{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_seven_languages", "label": "Lambda in Six Languages, and a Seventh", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Order, algebra, geometry, analysis, information and logic each name the same 976 cells; that a definition holds in every language and in their combinations is a standing requirement of the book, and Lambda is where it is met most completely."}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_binary_statement", "label": "The Binary Statement \u2014 Cells as 17-Bit Down-Sets", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It earns a seventh place by saying the cells ARE bit-vectors, which makes join and meet machine primitives rather than definitions \u2014 Birkhoff's correspondence in the language a machine reads."}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_surplus_in_implications", "label": "7.07 Surplus Bits Live in the Twenty Implications", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The twenty covering relations alone cut 131,072 words to exactly 976, so the surplus is not spare capacity and no bit is removable; redundancy in a closed index lives in the implications between bits, not in unused bits."}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_monotone_circuit", "label": "Lambda_8 Is a Monotone Boolean Circuit; Lambda_9 Is an Automaton", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With AND, OR and implication present but NOT, feedback and memory absent, Lambda_8 decides membership at depth five and cannot compute a function of successive inputs; closure under composition is what turns the decider into a machine at the ninth axis."}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_generating_function", "label": "F \u2014 The Single Generating Function", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_caterpillar", "label": "The Caterpillar Constraint Tree", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every row of A has exactly two non-zero entries, which is the single property making the graph a tree; a path of seven nodes with one pendant at k is why a linear left-to-right nesting with one bracketed factor exists at all."}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_pauli_coupling", "label": "The One Coupling g <= min(q, 4f+2) \u2014 the Pauli Principle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Removing the coupling turns 976 into 1,000 and the 24 excluded cells are all three electrons in an s orbital: every other bound is a counting or ordering fact, and this is the only physics and the only non-product term. It is recovered rather than assumed, since R(Lambda) = Lambda rebuilds it from the cells alone."}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_detachable_spin", "label": "2S Is a Leaf \u2014 Spin Multiplicity Algebraically Inert", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_rank_polynomial_asymmetry", "label": "Rank Polynomial Asymmetry and F(-1) = 2", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A rank polynomial is palindromic exactly when the poset is self-dual; the coordinates with two consecutive values would each contribute zero to the alternating sum if free, but the tree couples l to n and f to e so the vanishing factors never appear free and a residue of 2 survives."}, {"id": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_three_structural_facts", "label": "Why a Closed Expression Exists At All", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Monotone bounds give a polytope, two-variable bounds give a tree, and a tree's acyclicity gives factorisation; remove any one and no such expression exists \u2014 a sum bound produced 89,864 measured join failures, a three-variable constraint breaks treeness, and a cycle restores 2^d inclusion-exclusion terms."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_seven_languages", "target": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_binary_statement", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/REWRITE-chapter11-single-expression.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_binary_statement", "target": "recovered_rewrite_chapter11_single_expression_surplus_in_implications", 